review:
In the beginning i have to say that i've already played this game many times (and many versions) before, i've lost this count already. So i can justify this gem, alas it has little flaws.

First of all, its atmosphere. It's non-measurable for me because of this music (btw thanks for differing soundfonts option), visuals and gameplay, features devs chose to implement in this game make me wonder what if they could use modern tools but held old ambitions on...
That interactive world,
[list][*]where killed mutant can pull you back because he'd been running at your position before you shot him; 
[*]where you can lower damage received by your ranged enemy by changing your own pose (1994, guys) which you can set using screen's UI and forget about keybinds;
[*]where you can never find out that LG-XX Plasma Rifle can oneshot almost every enemy and even more than one by ONE SHOT (including yourself if you're too lucky to get that "lightning ball" ricochet) because you didn't even read manual and know nothing about that little suspicious slider;
[*]where you can throw that [strike]screen[/strike]earthshaker by unimaginable curve (i like these physics and thowing features) and slooowwwlyyy sip a cup of tea before your delayed shaker will divide that elite cyborg's precious plastic buttcheeks;
[*]where you can use only three-four (maximum is eight) types of your hardware (same for patches and explosives) because all another were added [strike]just for fun[/strike] by devs that loved cyberpunk and gifted you all reasonable abilities they could implement in this game;
[*]where you can follow died character's logs or reveal story of Citadel's stuff hopeless massacre and be surprised of this miserable end; 
[*]where you can forget about third of all weapons (all energetic types for example) you've found because you have to be quick with highest difficulty;
[*]where you can love AM-27 Flechette for its effectiveness and large pool of enemies that can drop rounds for it (even not the last obtainable gun ever) and do ratatata and where you can do zero shots of found gun till the end (because almost every walking metal trash pile drops plenty of rounds for Magnum and AM-27 and you'll never feel lack of it);
[*]where the heaviest and fearest enemy belongs to the easiest enemies (yeah i'm talking about you Cortex Reaver) and where you'll ♥♥♥♥ yourself when meet the smallest one (thanks devs for one of the Bridge's places);
[*]where only [strike]hacker[/strike] [strike]SHODAN[/strike] Abe Ghiran smiles at the end;
[*]where mutants will fear of you because you can sterilise med bay many times for that sweet medipatch (which is MUCH better than first aid kit);
[*]where you can find out that floor isn't that plain once you've obtained booster hardware;
[*]where lead pipe exists only because devs wanted you to shoot sometimes;
[*]where you can see spaces where you'll never get into in cyberspace;
[*]where you can do everything and meet almost no defy because you would spend hours trying to waste all of your available ammo and batteries;
[*]where you would keep your enemy alive as long as possible because of that really beautiful music;
[*]and so on and on and on, i can continue this endless foolish joke tirelessly, believe me.[/list]
So if you're stubborn enough then you can understand this love ode, or you can be impressed how rude was gamedev back in the SS's days and pass this game away, it's your choise dude. My only hope that it won't be forgotten at all.
